{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_018iJBS5hcLTypkZB7gAiKFx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! I can see the primary CTA is at line 159: \"Book via WhatsApp\". This is the button that the A/B test should target. \n\nNow let me understand the scope of the task properly before planning:\n\nBased on US-173 acceptance criteria:\n1. Vercel Edge Config store created and connected ✓ (already exists in the project)\n2. @vercel/edge-config and @vercel/flags packages installed (edge-config exists, need to add flags)\n3. A/B flag defined for /book page primary CTA copy (3 variants mentioned: 'Book Now' vs 'Check Availability' vs 'Get Best Price Direct')\n4. Flag evaluated in Next.js Middleware and variant cookie set before page render — zero layout shift\n5. GA4 custom dimension records which variant each session received\n6. Vercel Flags UI in dashboard shows flag status\n\nThe story was previously marked as oversized with 12854 lines diff. That was likely because they tried to do too much. Let me break this down into minimal scope:\n\n**Minimal implementation plan:**\n1. Create `site/src/lib/flags.ts` — define the A/B flag type and default flag values\n2. Create `site/src/middleware.ts` — read the flag, set a cookie with the variant\n3. Create `site/src/lib/useVariant.ts` — a server component hook/utility to read the variant cookie\n4. Modify `site/src/app/book/page.tsx` — conditionally render different CTA text based on variant\n5. Modify `site/src/components/BookEcommerceTracker.tsx` — set GA4 custom dimension for variant tracking\n6. Run `npm install @vercel/flags` (if not already installed)\n7. Test and verify\n\nLet me check what's the previous diff size issue by looking at git diff history.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1721,"cache_read_input_tokens":62711,"cache_creation":