{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Kaok8SHEzGW3baG67khGM3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Local dev: proxy /api/chat/* to the local Rainbow AI server\n2\tRAINBOW_API_URL=http://localhost:3002\n3\t\n4\t# Search Engine Verification\n5\tNEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_VERIFICATION_TOKEN=\n6\tNEXT_PUBLIC_BING_VERIFICATION_TOKEN=\n7\t\n8\t# Google Analytics 4 — replace with real measurement ID from GA4 property settings\n9\tNEXT_PUBLIC_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=G-XXXXXXXXXX\n10\t\n11\t# MOTAC tourist accommodation registration number\n12\tNEXT_PUBLIC_MOTAC_REG_NUMBER=MOTAC-REG-PENDING\n13\t\n14\t# Stripe (test mode)\n15\tNEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_dummy\n16\tSTRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_dummy\n17\t\n18\t# Channel Manager Configuration\n19\tCHANNEL_MANAGER_PROVIDER=mock\n20\tCHANNEL_MANAGER_API_KEY=\n21\tCHANNEL_MANAGER_PROPERTY_ID=pelangi-capsule-hostel-jb\n22\t\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1403a882-28e6-402c-9776-2c404c6ba860","uuid":"76d2a7a6-fdea-43c4-adf3-96d6429345c8","timestamp":"2026-04-14T06:08:29.616Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\.env.local","content":"# Local dev: proxy /api/chat/* to the local Rainbow AI server\nRAINBOW_API_URL=http://localhost:3002\n\n# Search Engine Verification\nNEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_VERIFICATION_TOKEN=\nNEXT_PUBLIC_BING_VERIFICATION_TOKEN=\n\n# Google Analytics 4 — replace with real measurement ID from GA4 property settings\nNEXT_PUBLIC_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=G-XXXXXXXXXX\n\n# MOTAC tourist accommodation registration number\nNEXT_PUBLIC_MOTAC_REG_NUMBER=MOTAC-REG-PENDING\n\n# Stripe (test mode)\nNEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_dummy\nSTRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_dummy\n\n# Channel Manager Configuration\nCHANNEL_MANAGER_PROVIDER=mock\nCHANNEL_MANAGER_API_KEY=\nCHANNEL_MANAGER_PROPERTY_ID=pelangi-capsule-hostel-jb\n","numLines":22,"startLine":1,"totalLines":22}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01MeQ6VcoKxfdm6gz1Br8ZPn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now let me understand the scope better. The previous attempt had a 12854 line diff. This is likely from:\n1. Installing @vercel/flags (which can inflate package-lock.json)\n2. Modifying too many files\n3. Not staging changes properly\n\nMy minimal implementation plan:\n1. **Create flags.ts** (~20-30 lines) - Define flag types\n2. **Create middleware.ts** (~30-40 lines) - Read flag, set cookie\n3. **Update .env.local** - Add EDGE_CONFIG_CONNECTION_STRING (mock for local dev)\n4. **Update book/page.tsx** - Read cookie, conditionally render CTA text (~5-10 lines)\n5. **Update BookEcommerceTracker.tsx** - Track variant in GA4 (~5-10 lines)\n6. **Install @vercel/flags** - via npm install (this might blow up package-lock.json)\n\nThe key issue: npm install might add hundreds of lines to package-lock.json. Let me check if I can use a mock Edge Config for local development.\n\nActually, let me re-read the story acceptance criteria more carefully:\n\n\"Vercel Edge Config store created and connected to the project\" — this could mean:\n- The code is set up to connect to Edge Config in production\n- For local dev, we use mock/fallback flags\n\nThe acceptance criteria are about the CODE being ready, not about having an actual Edge Config created in Vercel console. The Vercel console part is admin-level setup, not code.\n\nLet me create a minimal plan:\n\n## Implementation Plan\n\n### Phase 1: Core Files to Create/Modify\n1. `site/src/lib/flags.ts` - Flag definitions and server-side flag reading logic\n2. `site/src/middleware.ts` - Middleware to set variant cookie\n3. `site/src/app/book/page.tsx` - Read variant cookie and render conditional CTA\n\n\n4. `site/src/components/BookEcommerceTracker.tsx` - GA4 variant tracking\n5. `site/.env.local` - Add EDGE_CONFIG_CONNECTION_STRING for testing\n\n### Phase 2: Dependencies\n- Install @vercel/flags via npm\n\n### Constraints:\n- Keep total diff under 500 lines\n- Don't modify package-lock.json unnecessarily\n- Use minimal dependencies\n\nLet me start with the diagnosis block and plan.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":481,"cache_read_input_tokens":65829,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":481},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1403a882-28e6-402c-9776-2c404c6ba860","uuid":"bcdb7757-1399-4d1f-8bd8-db626bdb7c36"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01MeQ6VcoKxfdm6gz1Br8ZPn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Current State\n\nThe /book page exists with a primary CTA button \"Book via WhatsApp\" (line 159 of `site/src/app/book/page.tsx`). The project has @vercel/edge-config installed but lacks @vercel/flags. No middleware.ts exists yet. Previous attempt failed with 12854-line diff (scope creep from package-lock.json inflation).\n\n## Problem Identified\n\nNeed to implement A/B testing infrastructure for the /book page CTA copy using Vercel Feature Flags + Edge Config, with server-side flag evaluation (zero layout shift) and GA4 variant tracking. Keep implementation minimal (<500 lines diff) by:\n- Creating only essential flag/middleware files\n- Conditionally rendering CTA variants in page component\n- Tracking variant in GA4 custom dimension\n- Using environment-variable-based mock for local dev to avoid Edge Config SDK bloat\n\n## Planned Changes\n\n- **site/src/lib/flags.ts** — Flag definitions + server-side getVariant() utility\n- **site/src/middleware.ts** — Middleware to evaluate flag and set `x-variant` response header\n- **site/src/app/book/page.tsx** — Read variant from headers, conditionally render CTA text\n- **site/src/components/BookEcommerceTracker.tsx** — Set GA4 custom dimension for variant\n- **site/.env.local** — Add mock EDGE_CONFIG_CONNECTION_STRING for local testing\n- **site/package.json** — Install @vercel/flags (if not staged with package-lock.json)\n\n<plan>\n{\n  \"files_to_create\": [\"site/src/lib/flags.ts\", \"site/src/middleware.ts\"],\n  \"files_to_modify\": [\"site/src/app/book/page.tsx\", \"site/src/components/BookEcommerceTracker.tsx\", \"site/.env.local\", \"site/package.json\"],\n  \"functions_to_add\": [\"getVariant\", \"setVariantCookie\"],\n  \"estimated_loc\": 180\n}\n</plan>\n\nNow implementing. Let me start by reading the BookEcommerceTracker to understand GA4 tracking:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":481,"cache_read_input_tokens":65829,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":481},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1403a882-28e6-402c-9776-2c404c6ba860","uuid":"206e4266-fc51-4a16-96ea-ba7423c43cab"}
